.TH WSPANEL-UPDATE 8 "" "WSPanel" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
wspanel-update \- upgrade WSPanel to the newest release through apt
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wspanel-update
.RB [ \-\-pre | \-\-stable ]
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
apt follows the channel of the installed line (for example \fB1.2\fR), so
.B apt upgrade
brings fixes of that line only.
.B wspanel-update
points apt at the newest release (channel \fBstable\fR, or \fBpre\fR for
release candidates), installs the packages and runs
.BR wspanel-install (8),
which keeps the settings and sets the channel of the new line.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-pre
The newest release candidate, or release when newer (opt-in; the panel offers candidates only when
Testovací verze is switched on in Zabezpečení \(-> Aktualizace).
.TP
.B \-\-stable
The newest release: the default, also on a server that runs a release
candidate.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
No questions (the installer keeps the saved settings).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/wspanel.sources
The WSPanel apt repository and its channel.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wspanel-install (8)
